# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kept OUT of the Vercel upload.
#
# Vercel only needs: src/, tools/, package.json, vercel.json and public/ (which
# the build regenerates anyway). src/ and tools/ are deliberately NOT ignored —
# the build runs on Vercel and needs them.
#
# The site itself is served from public/, produced by `node tools/build.mjs`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Build output that Vercel regenerates during the build
public/

# Local tooling scratch space (headless Chrome profiles live here)
.verify/

# Git internals — Vercel clones the repo and must not receive this
.git/
.gitattributes
.gitignore

# GitHub-only files
.github/
DEPLOY.md

# Local environment and editor noise
.vercel/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vscode/
.idea/
node_modules/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT ignored on purpose: screenshots/, README.md, LICENSE, omarchy.html and
# index.html. They cost ~3 MB, well within limits, and keeping them makes the
# uploaded artifact self-documenting. The deployed site only serves public/,
# so they are storage rather than payload.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
